│ (300 mg); (2) carbamazepine (1,200 mg) and phenobarbital (300 mg); (3) phenytoin (300 mg) and phenobarbital (300     │
│ mg); or (4) carbamazepine (1,200 mg), with phenytoin (300 mg) and phenobarbital (300 mg). The treatment periods were │
│ separated by 2 wk of each patient\'s usual pre study medication. Treatment with all three drugs was the most         │
